--TEST--
`Core\Debug::coverage` lists each line that ran while coverage was on with its count and no line that did not, `stopCoverage` stops the counting and keeps the counts, and `startCoverage(true)` throws a `RuntimeError` naming `branch` when the mode leaves it out — `rule:testing/debug-surface`, `rule:testing/debug-mode-directive`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Debug::coverage
// covers: Core\Debug::startCoverage
// covers: Core\Debug::stopCoverage
class Calc {
    public static function double(int $n): int {
        return $n * 2;
    }
    public static function never(): int {
        return 0;
    }
}
// The mode turns coverage on before the first line. This stop turns it off,
// so only the lines between the start and the next stop are counted.
Core\Debug::stopCoverage();
echo Calc::double(1), "\n";
Core\Debug::startCoverage();
echo Calc::double(2), "\n";
echo Calc::double(3), "\n";
Core\Debug::stopCoverage();
echo Calc::double(4), "\n";

// The counts are kept after the stop: line 7 ran twice while coverage was on.
// Line 15 is counted because coverage was still on when it began, and line 17
// is not because it was off. Line 10 never ran, and nothing after line 20 is
// listed.
echo Core\Json::encode(Core\Debug::coverage()), "\n";

// Counting each side of a condition needs `branch` in the mode too.
try {
    Core\Debug::startCoverage(true);
    echo "branches started\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[debug]
mode = ["coverage"]
--EXPECT--
2
4
6
8
{"case.nvs":{"7":2,"15":1,"18":1,"19":1,"20":1}}
Core\Debug::startCoverage cannot start the `branch` probe, because `[debug] mode` does not include it.
help: add `"branch"` to `mode` under `[debug]` in nvs.toml. A server never runs a probe.
